-- §17 Every operation beside the notation position it names, or the fact that it names none.
#
# ONE ROW PER OPERATION, the whole dimension beside the restriction that crosses out of it.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ REPORTED AND NEVER ASSERTED, FOR §10b's REASON AT A DIFFERENT ADDRESS. A part reference
# that dangles is a VIOLATION and `checks/unresolved_part.sqlc` says so. An operation's
# `foreignId` cannot dangle or resolve, because there is nothing in this corpus for it to land
# on: it names a node in a BPMN document that travels beside the filing and is not held here.
# `pm:ForeignId`'s annotation refuses the lookup by name, so the only honest instrument is a
# report of who filed one.
#
# ⛔⛔ AND THE POPULATION IS THE FINDING, NOT THE CROSSING. Most operations name no position,
# and the corpus is thinner still: most FILINGS declare no operation at all. A reader who sees
# only the rows that cross would take this model for something that needs a process notation,
# and the shape of this table is the argument that it does not. ⭐ The BPMN is optional, and so
# is the logger that would fill it.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ AND THE ABSENT ARM IS WHY THIS FILE CHANGED SHAPE. It printed `(none named)` for every
# operation naming no position, which is the flattening this whole schema exists to refuse
# arriving in the report ABOUT the crossing. `pm:Operation/notationPosition` is required now and
# takes `pm:StatedForeignId`, so the reason is filed and this reads it: `none` is somebody looked
# and it is in no notation, `unmeasured` is a notation exists and nobody located this operation
# in it, `notApplicable` is this filing has no notation to point into. ⛔ The first is a finished
# answer and the second is work outstanding, and an untyped absence cannot tell them apart.
-- entries/operations.sqlc against entries/notation_references.sqlc, the whole beside the part.
SELECT o.filing                                       AS "filing!",
       o.label                                        AS "label!",
       coalesce(r.foreign_notation, '')               AS "notation!",
       coalesce(r.foreign_id, '')                     AS "node!",
       -- ⛔ NOT `coalesce(reason, 'stated')`: the two arms are exclusive by CHECK, so a row with
       --   neither is a load that should not have happened, and printing a word for it here would
       --   be this query answering for the document.
       coalesce(o.foreign_absent, '')                 AS "why_not!",
       (r.filing IS NOT NULL)                         AS "crosses!"
FROM      (
    :compose(entries/operations.sqlc)
) o
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(entries/notation_references.sqlc)
) r USING (filing, label)
ORDER BY (r.filing IS NOT NULL) DESC, 1, 2
